1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,890
This button doesn't exist.

2
00:00:01,930 --> 00:00:03,060
But you can FEEL it.

3
00:00:03,100 --> 00:00:05,250
Look. Nothing is touching his finger.

4
00:00:05,290 --> 00:00:06,920
So why can he feel a button?

5
00:00:06,960 --> 00:00:07,735
Under his hand,

6
00:00:07,775 --> 00:00:09,135
hundreds of tiny speakers

7
00:00:09,175 --> 00:00:10,700
fire ultrasound waves.

8
00:00:10,740 --> 00:00:12,320
They meet at one exact spot,

9
00:00:12,360 --> 00:00:14,040
making his skin feel pressure.

10
00:00:14,080 --> 00:00:14,940
Move that spot,

11
00:00:14,980 --> 00:00:16,290
and you can make an invisible button

12
00:00:16,330 --> 00:00:17,570
feel like it's moving.

13
00:00:17,610 --> 00:00:18,420
No glove.

14
00:00:18,460 --> 00:00:19,610
No physical button.

15
00:00:19,650 --> 00:00:21,325
Now imagine reaching into thin air

16
00:00:21,365 --> 00:00:23,330
and feeling the controls of your car.

17
00:00:23,370 --> 00:00:24,625
Or pressing a floating button

18
00:00:24,665 --> 00:00:26,040
without touching a screen.

19
00:00:26,080 --> 00:00:27,500
And here's the weird part.

20
00:00:27,540 --> 00:00:29,170
You can't actually grab it.

21
00:00:29,210 --> 00:00:30,940
But your skin can still feel it.

